      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing is the crushing weight of profound grief, and it makes perfect sense that you feel like a mistake when the world feels so irrevocably changed. You don't have to be \"okay\" right now; you just have to be where you are. Acknowledging that your existence feels like a debt is a heavy truth, but it's also a sign that you feel things deeply. If you can, allow yourself to feel that emptiness without judgment, and know that letting go of the pressure to \"move on\" is a necessary first step.",
